Cell["\<\
Lower-level functions for counting critical points and locating singularities.\
\>", "TechNoteCaption",
 CellID->1642276539,ExpressionUUID->"f4785062-351a-48a9-8931-76bcbc81ec5b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Counting Critical Points", "Subsection",
 CellID->505260736,ExpressionUUID->"19449a6b-7b28-4a48-a26c-ab9bfa1a9fd9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first of these is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CountSectorsUnregulated"]], 
    "paclet:DiscKosky/ref/CountSectorsUnregulated", 
    "DiscKosky Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "3cabde1c-74f7-4dd0-a40e-0bd2244f639c"],
 ", which computes the number of critical points in each sector. It takes as \
input a Lee\[Dash]Pomeransky polynomial, a list of integration variables, and \
a set of propagators to cut. The result is the number of critical points in \
each sector above the specified cut."
}], "TechNoteText",
 CellID->456666947,ExpressionUUID->"1bf66865-216f-463b-989d-0f1f29dba94e"],

Cell["\<\
Count the critical points of the two-mass easy box, with no propagators cut:\
\>", "TechNoteMathCaption",
 CellID->811259901,ExpressionUUID->"772493cb-4880-4fc3-a560-3d026cafe030"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

