 CellID->1590554349,ExpressionUUID->"7b950d72-0cc7-457e-8eeb-996030e9e4d8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The first element of the output is the total number of critical points \
(summed over all sectors that are consistent with the specified cut), while \
the second indicates how these critical points are distributed among the \
different sectors. The third element gives the list of sectors that label the \
critical point counts in the second element.\
\>", "TechNoteText",
 CellID->822751505,ExpressionUUID->"afeec132-e931-4f16-aaa0-fe278bc2ace3"],

Cell["\<\
If a non-empty cut is specified, the function simply ignores any sectors that \
do not survive on the support of that cut.\
\>", "TechNoteText",
 CellID->1041466535,ExpressionUUID->"b95a816c-e99a-4f68-b65c-9177d3c37478"],

Cell["\<\
Count only the critical points that survive when all four propagators are cut:\
\>", "TechNoteMathCaption",
 CellID->995489754,ExpressionUUID->"c07ba6e9-5706-4315-8bf1-b76136d5940d"],

