    "index" -> True, "label" -> "Disc Kosky Tech Note", "language" -> "en", 
    "paclet" -> "DiscKosky", "status" -> "None", "summary" -> 
    "DiscKosky is a package for studying the repeated discontinuity structure \
of Euler integrals. This is done primarily by counting the number of critical \
points associated to the Feynman integral. This tech note introduces the most \
important commands of DiscKosky, illustrated on a simple one-loop example. \
More details on each function and its options can be found on the \
corresponding reference pages. DiscKosky provides three main high-level \
functions for predicting sequential discontinuities: \
CheckDoubleDiscontinuities, CheckSequentialDiscontinuity, and \
SectorDropGraph.", "synonyms" -> {}, "tabletags" -> {}, "title" -> 
